"flower": "Wild rose",
"story": [
"Alberta is where the endless, golden prairies abruptly smash into the dramatic, jagged teeth of the Rocky Mountains. It’s a province of brilliant contrasts, where you can wander through the dusty, dinosaur-bone-littered canyons of the Badlands one day, and paddle a canoe across the impossibly turquoise, glacier-fed waters of Lake Louise the next. The sky feels bigger here, stretching wide over fields of canola before snapping your attention to the snow-capped horizon.",
"Culturally, Alberta beats with the heart of a cowboy but moves with the hustle of a modern boomtown. It’s the undisputed rodeo capital, peaking every summer with the raucous Calgary Stampede, yet it’s also home to Edmonton's sprawling, eclectic arts and theater festivals. The people here are fiercely proud, hardworking, and deeply welcoming, offering a blend of rugged frontier spirit and sleek, cosmopolitan energy."
],
