"joined": 1905,
"flower": "Western red lily",
"story": [
"They call Saskatchewan the \"Land of the Living Skies,\" and once you’ve seen a sunset here, you’ll understand exactly why. The horizon seems entirely uninterrupted, offering a 360-degree canvas for violent, beautiful summer thunderstorms and twilight colors that bleed across the atmosphere like watercolors. While outsiders often dismiss it as just \"flat,\" those who look closer find rolling hills, hidden valleys, and a surprising number of serene, pine-fringed lakes in the north.",
"There’s an undeniable warmth to the people that makes this province truly special. It’s the kind of place where a broken-down car on a gravel road will result in three different farmers pulling over to help you within ten minutes. Saskatoon pulses with an unexpectedly hip, culinary-driven riverfront scene, while the entire province unites under a shared, almost religious devotion to their football team, the Roughriders."
],
