"type": "Province",
"region": "prairies",
"capital": "Winnipeg",
"largest": "Winnipeg",
"joined": 1870,
"flower": "Prairie crocus",
"story": [
"Manitoba is Canada’s beating geographic heart, a place where extreme seasons carve out some of the country's most spectacular wildlife encounters. Up north in Churchill, the tundra meets the icy waters of Hudson Bay, offering a front-row seat to migrating polar bears and pods of ghostly white beluga whales. Further south, the province is scarred by massive, ocean-like lakes and thick boreal forests that turn into a fiery explosion of color every autumn.",
"Winnipeg, the gritty and resilient capital, is an absolute cultural powerhouse that punches way above its weight class. It’s a city bursting with world-class indie music, a booming culinary scene, and a profound connection to its deep Indigenous and French-Canadian roots at places like The Forks. Manitobans are tough—they have to be to survive the biting winters—but that shared resilience breeds a community that is incredibly tight-knit and fiercely creative."
],
